    "UIName": "Kharon",
    "Id": "chassisdef_kharon_KHN-Vilthos",
    "Name": "Kharon",
    "Details": "The pilot of this Kharon variant is a captured Ghost Bear warrior whose tactical acumen was deemed far too valuable for the Society to simply waste through execution. Though remarkably old for a Clan warrior, Vilthos Magnusson remained far too effective to be relegated to a Solahma unit, a fact his captors were quick to exploit. Vilthos is by no means a willing member of the Society, but extensive neural implant surgery, repeated courses of mutagenic therapy, and the surgical amputation of his limbs allowed Society scientists to permanently integrate what remained of the former Ghost Bear directly into the Mech's new torso-mounted cockpit. The results have exceeded expectations, transforming Vilthos into a remarkably effective tool whose connection to the Kharon extends far beyond that of a conventional MechWarrior. Some peculiarities remain, however. Society warriors assigned to formations alongside Vilthos have repeatedly complained of hearing him muttering over the tactical network throughout combat, seemingly oblivious to those around him: 'Optimize... optimize... optimize...'\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Combat Computer</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.18</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limit: Right Upper</color>",
    "Icon": "Kharon"
  },
  "VariantName": "KHN-Vilthos",
